From bd806e6601740854848c6fd276c8015aba6b604c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyperminer <admin@blazecoin.co.uk>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:53:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Post-quantum key-hash output as witness version 2 (regtest
 sketch): OP_2 <32-byte hash> committing to an ML-DSA-44 key blob, witness
 <signature> <keyblob>, BIP-341-shaped message with ext_flag 2 under the tag
 PQSighash, SIGHASH_DEFAULT only, FIPS 204 context string bitcoin-pq-v1; BIP9
 deployment pq (always active on regtest, never elsewhere); SCRIPT_VERIFY_PQ
 in the consensus and standard flag sets; a spend of the new program is
 standard only where the deployment is active; the BIP-341 single hashes are
 precomputed for the new program as for Taproot; dust priced from the
 3,740-byte witness; vendored pq-crystals reference with deterministic
 signing; unit tests (5 cases, 9 mutations, weight 3,904 WU per input, dust
 3,057 sat) and a two-node functional test (honest spend mined at 3,904 WU per
 input, bad-signature block accepted by the old-rules node and rejected by the
 upgraded node, mempool mutations, dust). Not a proposal; not scheduled on any
 live network.

Besides the interpreter, four places had to learn the new program: relay policy (a spend is a standard input only where the deployment is active), the BIP-341 precomputation, DeferringSignatureChecker (it forwards CheckPQSignature to the checker it wraps, as it does the Schnorr check; left to the base class it returned false for every spend of the new program), and the list of all consensus script flags (GetAllConsensusScriptFlags includes SCRIPT_VERIFY_PQ where the deployment is enabled, to agree with GetBlockScriptFlags and CONSENSUS_SCRIPT_VERIFY_FLAGS).

Three existing functional tests change, because on regtest witness version 2 with a 32-byte program is now defined and the deployment is listed: p2p_segwit.py uses a 33-byte program for version 2, feature_taproot.py skips that one shape, and rpc_blockchain.py expects the pq deployment and the PQ flag in getdeploymentinfo.
